{title: Never to Last}
{lyricist: Sergio Rykov}
{composer: Sergio Rykov}

{comment_italic: Dedicated to the earthquake in Lisbon on 26.08.2024}

{start_of_verse}
With a trembling hand, I hold the pen,
Slowly in beat, I write again.
Let it fly high, no boundaries faced,
Heartbeats loud, no return to trace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I see the sky up above me here,
Stars below me, sparkling clear.
Whispers soft all around, everywhere,
Life can’t be split beyond repair.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
Now and then, all’s in the past,
Here and there - never to last.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse}
Days and weeks already count down,
Our world tense like us, waiting round.
The dawn’s shape still blurred and gray,
We’re apart, drifting away.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
The planet trembles, the waves collide,
Washing the dirt from all sides.
The air is charged, it’s buzzing loud,
No strength left, breaking free somehow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: label="Spoken"}
Despite all this pain, may joy come into our lives.
The joy of a simple day, to live all that the world brings to us,
In acceptance and awareness - there is nothing we cannot face together.
Without breaking ourselves, each other, or the planet that shelters us.
{end_of_verse}
